{
    "_DESCRIPTION": "Nitrogen cycle with explicit dissolved oxygen and dissolved organic carbon. Redox rates are limited by the electron donor and acceptor (Monod), by inhibition (O2 on denitrification) and by the Gibbs energy of the reaction through the thermodynamic factor F_T of Jin and Bethke (2003, 2005). Activities are approximated by molar concentrations and the pH is prescribed (pH_w). Formulation RN-T of the OpenWQ PHREEQC paper. Variant _gs: soil plant uptake of NO3 and NH4 follows a growing-season heat-unit response, k_pu * clip((T - T_base_pu)/(T_opt_pu - T_base_pu), 0, 1) * N with T_base_pu 5 C and T_opt_pu 25 C, instead of k_pu * theta_T^(T-20) * N; everything else is identical to the base template.",
    "_UNITS": "Species symbols are masses in the engine (g; as N for NO3-N and NH4-N, as O2 for DO, as C for DOC). Vw_m3 is the water volume of the cell (m3), so species/Vw_m3 is mg/L. Rates are written per unit volume (mg/L/day) and multiplied by Vw_m3 to give g/day.",
    "_REFERENCES": [
        "Jin and Bethke (2003, 2005) thermodynamic factor",
        "Henze et al. (2000) ASM half-saturation and inhibition constants",
        "Stumm and Morgan (1996) Gibbs energies of formation",
        "Benson and Krause (1984) O2 saturation"
    ],
    "_TO_CHECK": "Constants are indicative values from the references above; m_ATP and chi are illustrative. For these three reactions F_T stays close to 1 except near depletion of a reactant.",
    "MODULE_NAME": "NATIVE_BGC_FLEX",
    "CHEMICAL_SPECIES": {
        "LIST": {
            "1": "NO3-N",
            "2": "NH4-N",
            "3": "DO",
            "4": "DOC",
            "5": "N2_loss",
            "6": "CO2_loss",
            "7": "NH3_loss",
            "8": "PLANT_N"
        },
        "BGC_GENERAL_MOBILE_SPECIES": [
            "NO3-N",
            "NH4-N",
            "DO",
            "DOC"
        ],
        "_LIST_DESCRIPTIONS": {
            "NO3-N": "Nitrate as N",
            "NH4-N": "Ammonium as N",
            "DO": "Dissolved oxygen as O2",
            "DOC": "Dissolved organic carbon as C",
            "N2_loss": "Dinitrogen produced (sink)",
            "CO2_loss": "CO2 produced (sink)",
            "NH3_loss": "Volatilized ammonia (sink)",
            "PLANT_N": "Plant uptake (sink)"
        }
    },
    "GLOBAL_PARAMETERS": {
